// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6459 new: COM TypeLib hijack via scriptlet moniker + script runtime loaded by Explorer
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6459
// Pull request author: redsand
// Change: new rule
// Title: COM TypeLib Hijack Via Scriptlet Or Remote Moniker
// Sigma ID: a077d7ab-3c9c-41d9-a1e7-db2c78cabe1e
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Tim Shelton (HAWK.io)
// Date: 2026-10-13 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1546.015
// Description: Detects a type library whose win32/win64 path is set to a "script:" moniker, a ".sct" scriptlet
//   or a URL. Type libraries are registered to DLL, OCX or TLB files. Windows resolves a "script:"
//   path through scrobj.dll and runs the scriptlet in whichever process loads the type library.
//   Attackers register the hijack under the user's own HKCU\Software\Classes\TypeLib (no admin
//   rights needed) for a type library that Explorer loads at logon, such as the Microsoft Scriptlet
//   Library {EAB22AC0-30C1-11CF-A7EB-0000C05BAE0B}.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://cicada-8.medium.com/hijack-the-typelib-new-com-persistence-technique-32ae1d284661
//   - https://reliaquest.com/blog/threat-spotlight-hijacked-and-hidden-new-backdoor-and-persistence-technique/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/16c482306186f8827fdb39c72ba5f76b1a521d55/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_typelib_script_moniker.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\TypeLib.*$" and (RegistryKey contains "\\win32" or RegistryKey contains "\\win64") and ((RegistryValueData startswith "script:" or RegistryValueData startswith "http:" or RegistryValueData startswith "https:") or RegistryValueData contains ".sct")
